====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|informal|transitive}} To perform a cursory investigation of; [[scope out]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Don Harris|title=The Drunk|passage=We don't know, so let's '''scope''' the action before having another shoot out.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Khalid Patel|title=Hollow Shotguns|passage=“Let's '''scope''' the scene.” The gang advanced, searching for humanity.}}
# {{lb|en|medicine|colloquial}} To [[perform]] any [[medical]] [[procedure]] that ends in the suffix {{m|en|-scopy}}, such as {{m|en|endoscopy}}, {{m|en|colonoscopy}}, {{m|en|bronchoscopy}}, etc.
#: {{ux|en|The surgeon will '''scope''' the football player's knee to repair damage to a ligament.}}
# To define the scope of something.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|title=An Introduction to Characterizing Sites Contaminated with DNAPLs|page=10
|text=Before '''scoping''' the investigation and developing a work plan, it is necessary to establish reasonable goals and objectives.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2018-01-19|author=Judith Seddon|title=Practitioner's Guide to Global Investigations|publisher=Law Business Research Ltd.|isbn=9781912377831
|text=The purpose of witness interviews is multi-faceted but generally includes '''scoping''' the investigation, understanding the facts and issues at play, and assessing the accountability of individuals and possible defences for the company and{{nb...}}}}
# {{lb|en|programming}} To limit (an object or variable) to a certain [[region]] of program [[source code]].
#: {{ux|en|If we locally '''scope''' the user's login name, it won't be accessible from outside this function.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} To examine under a microscope.
#: {{ux|en|The entomologist explained that he could not tell what species of springtail we were looking at without '''scoping''' it.}}
# {{lb|en|birdwatching|informal}} To observe a bird using a [[spotting scope]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=w:Sean Dooley|title=The Big Twitch|publisher=Allen and Unwin|location=Sydney|page=199|passage=`Maybe there was another darker bird and it had flown away before we could '''scope''' it?' `Yes there must have been,' came the grim-faced reply.}}

